      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Using a strong dose of ibuprofen might not address the underlying infection, and hydrogen peroxide can sometimes irritate damaged skin, potentially worsening the inflammation. These home remedies are not a substitute for medical evaluation when symptoms like warmth and pain are present. For temporary comfort, keep the area clean and try to keep it dry, but please prioritize seeing a doctor as soon as your schedule allows.",
      "source": "target",
